Track: Subtitle Inventory Disk Import Recovery

Summary:
- Repaired the subtitle movie/series scan endpoints so they now perform a real filesystem scan for sidecar subtitle files beside existing variant video files.
- Added disk-scan logic to SubtitleInventoryApiService that imports supported sidecar extensions into VariantSubtitleTrack, preserves embedded tracks, and reports accurate subtitlesFound/newSubtitles counts.
- Added route-level regression tests for movie scan, series scan, and idempotent repeat scans.
- Created and archived the dedicated Conductor repair track for this bug fix.

Verification:
- Passed: npm test -- server/src/api/routes/subtitleRoutes.scan.test.ts
- Passed: npm test -- server/src/api/routes/subtitleRoutes.scan.test.ts server/src/services/SubtitleInventoryApiService.test.ts server/src/api/routes/subtitleRoutes.phase3.test.ts

Why:
- The previous /api/subtitles/*/scan routes only read existing DB inventory and always returned newSubtitles: 0, so already-downloaded subtitle files on disk were never imported into the database.
